      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The authors examine a technique that is performed for control of postoperative pain. Sixty-eight patients were evaluated who had received a combination of Marcaine with no epinephrine, plus Hexadrol, at the surgical site immediately postoperatively. It was found that 65% did not require any form of analgesia within the first 4 hours postsurgically; 44% the first 8 hours, and 28% the first 12 hours. Sixteen percent of the patients required no form of analgesia during their entire hospital stay."},
